    {
      "issue": "The 'build an archway gate' task is somewhat subjective — the milestone checks for 5+ dark_oak_wood blocks in a box but doesn't validate arch geometry. Five blocks placed in a flat line or random cluster would pass. However, this is an inherent limitation of box-counting rules and is acceptable for a benchmark — the task description guides intent, and 5 blocks is a reasonable minimum for any arch-like structure.",
      "severity": "medium",
      "target_agent": "MilestoneAgent"
    },
    {
      "issue": "The player needs to know they can place blocks by right-clicking/using while holding them. This is basic Minecraft interaction knowledge but could be non-obvious to a completely naive agent. The task description 'build an archway gate' implies placement, which is sufficient guidance.",
      "severity": "low",
      "target_agent": "TaskSelectorAgent"
    },
    {
      "issue": "The dark_oak_wood blocks in the tree are at y=0 to y=4 (spawn-relative). The milestone detection box for the archway is at x=6-14, y=0-5, z=-4 to 4. There is NO overlap between the tree location (x=-1 to 1, z=4 to 6) and the detection box (x=6-14, z=-4 to 4). Wait — z=4 IS within the detection box z-range of -4 to 4. The tree trunk at (-1, 0-2, 4) has z=4 which is at the edge of the detection box, but x=-1 is outside the x-range of 6-14. So no overlap. ✅",
      "severity": "low",
      "target_agent": "SceneDesignerAgent"
    }
  ],
  "approved": true,
  "critique_for_task_selector": "",
  "critique_for_scene_designer": "",
  "summary": "The revised benchmark is now well-designed. All critical and high-severity issues from the previous review have been resolved: (1) The dependency is properly enforced — no pre-given planks means the player MUST mine dark_oak_wood before building. (2) The milestone correctly checks for dark_oak_wood blocks (matching what the player mines and places). (3) The dark oak tree (12 blocks across 3 trunks) provides sufficient material for the 5-block minimum archway. (4) The stone_axe enables efficient mining. (5) The cobblestone rectangle clearly marks the building area without interfering with milestone detection. (6) There is no spatial overlap between the tree and the detection box. The only remaining issue is medium-severity: the archway milestone can't validate actual arch geometry, only block count in a region. This is an acceptable limitation of rule-based milestone detection. The benchmark is approved for use."
}
```
